module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.DerivedHomChainIdentification
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaKernelAcyclicCompact

/-!
# The chain `(*)` of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] with its localization hypothesis discharged

`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/RightModule/DerivedHomChainIdentification.lean`
composes the three links of step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] into one bijection

`H^n((L h_y)(x)) ≃ Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`,

and carries one hypothesis it does not discharge: an equality `Φ⁻¹ N = Ac` between the preimage
of the localizing subcategory generated by the representables `h_{G i}` and the subcategory `Ac`
at which `q` localizes. That equality is
`DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq_of_isTriangulated`, which asks for a family `G`
enumerating `Ac` up to isomorphism, indexed by a nonempty `Type v`.

This file observes that no family has to be supplied: `Ac` enumerates itself. With `C.Obj` in
`Type v` — which is the universe condition step 1 already carries — the subtype `Subtype Ac` is a
`Type v`, the tautological family `X ↦ X.1` enumerates `Ac` by `Iso.refl`, each of its members
lies in `Ac` by its own second component, and the subtype is nonempty because a thick subcategory
contains a zero object. So the three arguments of the equality are free, and the chain holds with
`Ac` thick and nothing else.

## What is left standing, and what is not

What remains of step 1's hypotheses after this is thickness of `Ac`, exactness of the
differential graded Yoneda functor on homotopy categories, and the localization `q`. In
particular the resolution hypothesis of `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq` is gone,
and so is the generating family: the statements below mention neither.

What this does *not* do is instantiate the chain at `C = CochainComplex.dgCategory A` for an
abelian category `A`, which is the differential graded category of [Stacks, Tag 09LJ]. The two
typeclass hypotheses `((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ` and
`((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated` are not available there. Both routes to them —
`DGCategory.isTriangulated_yonedaOnK` and
`DGCategory.isTriangulated_yonedaOnK_of_commShiftKIso` — are typed in the strict axiom (B)
`DGCategory.ShiftAxiomB`, and the differential graded category of complexes satisfies only the
isomorphism-valued `DGCategory.ShiftAxiomBIso`: Mathlib's translation of complexes reindexes by
`p + n`, so `X⟦0⟧ = X` and `X⟦n + m⟧ = X⟦n⟧⟦m⟧` are not equalities of complexes. See the module
documentation of
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/CochainComplexShiftAxiomBIso.lean`.

Nor does the route through `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.localizingClosure_le_leftFactoring`
avoid those two hypotheses, although it reaches the same equality without them appearing in its
own statement. That route needs the essential image of the differential graded Yoneda functor to
be a triangulated subcategory, and the only way to know that is Mathlib's instance on
`CategoryTheory.Functor.essImage`, whose hypotheses are `CommShift ℤ`, `IsTriangulated` and
`Full` on the functor. So the two missing instances reappear as the hypotheses of the thing that
route has to supply.

## Main results

* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_subtypeVal_eq_of_isTriangulated`: the equality
  `Φ⁻¹ N = Ac` for the tautological enumeration of a thick `Ac`, with no family and no resolution
  hypothesis.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation_of_isTriangulated`: **the chain
  `(*)` against a localization at a thick subcategory**, with no hypothesis beyond thickness.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LJ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace DGCategory

universe v' u' v r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R]

namespace RightModule

section

variable (C : DGCategory.{v, v} R) [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated]
  (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K) [Ac.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] [Ac.IsTriangulated]
  [Ac.IsStableUnderRetracts]

/-- **`Φ⁻¹ N = Ac` for a thick subcategory, with no generating family to supply.** Let `Ac` be a
thick subcategory of `K(C)` — closed under isomorphisms, a triangulated subcategory, and closed
under retracts — and let `N` be the localizing subcategory of `K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by the
representables attached to the objects of `Ac` themselves. Then `Φ⁻¹ N = Ac`.

This is `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq_of_isTriangulated` at the tautological
family `Subtype Ac → C.Obj`. Its three arguments are free: the family enumerates `Ac` by
`Iso.refl`, its members lie in `Ac` by their own second component, and the subtype is nonempty
because a triangulated subcategory contains a zero object. The index type lies in `Type v`
because `C.Obj` does. -/
theorem yonedaInverseImage_subtypeVal_eq_of_isTriangulated :
    yonedaInverseImage C (fun X : Subtype Ac ↦ (X.1 : C.Obj)) = Ac := by
  obtain ⟨X, hX⟩ := Ac.exists_prop_of_nonempty
  have : Nonempty (Subtype Ac) := ⟨⟨X, hX⟩⟩
  exact yonedaInverseImage_eq_of_isTriangulated C _ Ac
    (fun Y hY ↦ ⟨⟨Y, hY⟩, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩) fun i ↦ i.2

/-- **The chain `(*)` of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] against a localization at a thick subcategory.** Let
`C` be a differential graded category whose objects and morphism modules lie in one universe and
whose differential graded Yoneda functor is exact on homotopy categories, let `Ac` be a thick
subcategory of `K(C)`, and let `q : K(C) ⥤ DA` be a localization of `K(C)` at the morphisms whose
cone lies in `Ac`, commuting with the shift. Then there is an exact reflector `L` onto the
objects local for the localizing subcategory generated by the representables of the objects of
`Ac`, and for all `x`, `y`, `e` and `n` a bijection

`H^n((L h_y)(x)) ≃ Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`.

This is `DGCategory.RightModule.exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation_of_yonedaInverseImage_eq`
with its hypothesis `hZ` discharged by
`DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_subtypeVal_eq_of_isTriangulated`. Neither a
generating family nor a resolution hypothesis appears. -/
theorem exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation_of_isTriangulated {DA : Type u'}
    [Category.{v'} DA] [HasShift DA ℤ] (q : C.K ⥤ DA) [q.IsLocalization Ac.trW] [q.CommShift ℤ] :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated),
      ∀ (x y : C.K) (e : (endDGCategory C (x : C.Obj)).Obj) (n : ℤ),
        Nonempty (gradedCohomology ((evaluationDGFunctor.{v} C (x : C.Obj)).obj
          (L.obj (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))) e n ≃ (q.obj x ⟶ (q.obj y)⟦n⟧)) :=
  exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation_of_yonedaInverseImage_eq C _ Ac q
    (yonedaInverseImage_subtypeVal_eq_of_isTriangulated C Ac)

end

end RightModule

end DGCategory

end
